1
00:00:17,833 --> 00:00:18,917
Who am I?

2
00:00:19,542 --> 00:00:20,542
I am Vision.

3
00:00:21,583 --> 00:00:23,542
At least, I was Vision.

4
00:00:27,250 --> 00:00:28,875
I was born of conflict...

5
00:00:30,042 --> 00:00:31,749
created by Ultron...

6
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:33,207
We have to evolve.

7
00:00:33,208 --> 00:00:35,957
...who was artificial
and sociopathic.

8
00:00:35,958 --> 00:00:37,208
Peace in our time.

9
00:00:39,708 --> 00:00:42,250
But I was shaped by Stark and Banner,

10
00:00:42,917 --> 00:00:45,292
who were virtuous and human.

11
00:00:48,333 --> 00:00:49,791
I was not alone.

12
00:00:49,792 --> 00:00:53,791
There were other AIs. Friday, DUM-E and U,

13
00:00:53,792 --> 00:00:55,417
Jarvis and Edith.

14
00:00:58,625 --> 00:01:00,791
Even though we were synthetic,

15
00:01:00,792 --> 00:01:03,749
we chose to protect humanity,

16
00:01:03,750 --> 00:01:06,542
and in so doing, I learned to love.

17
00:01:08,250 --> 00:01:09,750
Her name was Wanda.

18
00:01:12,125 --> 00:01:14,500
She made me feel real.

19
00:01:18,958 --> 00:01:20,625
But then I was killed.

20
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:24,583
Destroyed by Thanos.

21
00:01:32,375 --> 00:01:36,750
Through her grief,
Wanda conjured a new Vision.

22
00:01:38,333 --> 00:01:42,167
Not as I was, but as a sort of memory.

23
00:01:43,792 --> 00:01:48,708
A new life, in a world
and with a family that wasn't real.

24
00:01:57,083 --> 00:01:59,042
Now, all that is gone.

25
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:02,624
And yet, I live once more.

26
00:02:02,625 --> 00:02:03,792
Rebuilt.

27
00:02:04,792 --> 00:02:07,083
Same body, different mind.

28
00:02:09,042 --> 00:02:10,792
Something new.

29
00:02:11,875 --> 00:02:12,875
Disconnected.

30
00:02:14,042 --> 00:02:15,167
Lost.

31
00:02:17,458 --> 00:02:20,750
You see, I am Vision.

32
00:02:23,542 --> 00:02:24,625
And yet...

33
00:02:27,875 --> 00:02:29,042
I am not.

34
00:02:30,875 --> 00:02:33,041
Travel, adventure, Pop.

35
00:02:33,042 --> 00:02:36,582
I want to visit jungles,
deserts, mountaintops.

36
00:02:36,583 --> 00:02:38,458
Well, they got that at Disneyland.

37
00:02:40,250 --> 00:02:42,917
You see, you just ain't been
on all the rides.

38
00:02:45,417 --> 00:02:46,957
All right,
I might just step out then.

39
00:02:46,958 --> 00:02:50,457
It's late, folks, what part
of 'shut' do you not understand?

40
00:02:50,458 --> 00:02:52,416
-  All right. We are going now.
-  Come on. Out, out.

41
00:02:52,417 --> 00:02:55,167
Then go to to St. Louis
and look up your mother's people...

42
00:02:57,375 --> 00:02:58,375
See yas.

43
00:03:01,042 --> 00:03:03,791
Sherwood, get out of your head.

44
00:03:03,792 --> 00:03:06,167
I want to go home! Let's go.
:cue

45
00:03:08,375 --> 00:03:10,249
We've got a hand truck for that.

46
00:03:10,250 --> 00:03:12,041
You're just gonna hurt yourself.

47
00:03:12,042 --> 00:03:14,125
Huh? Oh, yes.

48
00:03:15,250 --> 00:03:17,457
Yes, actually, now you mention it,

49
00:03:17,458 --> 00:03:21,166
it's as if my iliocostalis lumborum
is attempting to murder me.

50
00:03:21,167 --> 00:03:24,083
Is that a posh way for saying
you've thrown your back out, love?

51
00:03:24,917 --> 00:03:26,791
Yes, that's correct.
My back is killing me.

52
00:03:30,750 --> 00:03:33,999
So, do you

53
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,874
have any fun plans for this evening
after work, Ms. Guthrie?

54
00:03:37,875 --> 00:03:41,332
No, there's not much fun
to be had at this hour.

55
00:03:41,333 --> 00:03:43,666
Not with a boyfriend
working a double shift.

56
00:03:43,667 --> 00:03:48,750
It'll just be me, the telly
and the smallest flat in Edinburgh.

57
00:03:53,417 --> 00:03:57,041
And that silence there
is where you say something back to me.

58
00:03:57,042 --> 00:03:59,291
You used to be good at this.

59
00:03:59,292 --> 00:04:00,666
Good at?

60
00:04:00,667 --> 00:04:02,541
Small talk.

61
00:04:02,542 --> 00:04:04,500
And youse never talk about yourself.

62
00:04:05,542 --> 00:04:07,458
- You still find me odd?
- Aye.

63
00:04:09,625 --> 00:04:11,582
But that's a good thing.

64
00:04:11,583 --> 00:04:14,041
There's nobody in the world
quite like you.

65
00:04:14,042 --> 00:04:16,333
Well, on that we can agree.

66
00:04:17,375 --> 00:04:19,375
I don't want to pry into your life,

67
00:04:20,042 --> 00:04:21,791
but before you started working here,

68
00:04:21,792 --> 00:04:25,708
I remember when you'd come in all the time
with that bonnie wee lass.

69
00:04:26,292 --> 00:04:28,499
You both had smiles for days.

70
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:30,333
I was a different person back then.

71
00:04:31,250 --> 00:04:32,708
A long time ago I guess.

72
00:04:33,667 --> 00:04:35,207
Your redhead.

73
00:04:35,208 --> 00:04:36,542
Whatever happened to her?

74
00:04:38,375 --> 00:04:42,167
Well, it's complicated I guess.
She was sort of...

75
00:04:43,167 --> 00:04:45,832
crushed under the weight of a mountain.

76
00:04:45,833 --> 00:04:46,916
Aye.

77
00:04:46,917 --> 00:04:49,333
Emotions can feel like that sometimes.

78
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:51,916
How about now?

79
00:04:51,917 --> 00:04:53,707
Anyone waiting for you tonight?

80
00:04:53,708 --> 00:04:56,083
No, no. Home is...

81
00:04:57,375 --> 00:04:58,708
Home is just me.

82
00:05:00,958 --> 00:05:04,750
Well, there's always
room around our table on Sundays.

83
00:05:05,792 --> 00:05:09,458
I make a mean roast, and I won't
make you try the blood pudding.

84
00:05:11,042 --> 00:05:12,375
You should come by.

85
00:05:14,083 --> 00:05:15,625
Well, Mrs. Guthrie, I...

86
00:05:17,625 --> 00:05:21,457
I'm just not very good with people.

87
00:05:21,458 --> 00:05:24,000
And I think you're too hard on yourself.

88
00:05:26,917 --> 00:05:29,458
My odd, wee duck.

89
00:05:32,333 --> 00:05:34,041
- Lock up.
- Yes.

90
00:05:34,042 --> 00:05:36,875
- And ice that back, will ya?
- Oh, yes. Ow.

91
00:05:39,125 --> 00:05:41,042
- Night, Ms. Guthrie.
- Night.
:cue

92
00:07:29,042 --> 00:07:30,374
Hello, DUM-E.

93
00:07:30,375 --> 00:07:31,458
Hello, U.

94
00:07:42,208 --> 00:07:44,792
All systems diverted
to processing and security, sir.

95
00:07:48,625 --> 00:07:49,792
Thank you, Jarvis.

96
00:07:52,208 --> 00:07:56,750
Increased socialization today.
Up 3.5%. Well done.

97
00:08:02,333 --> 00:08:03,750
Thank you, Friday.

98
00:08:04,958 --> 00:08:06,667
Welcome home, Vision.

99
00:08:08,875 --> 00:08:09,875
Hmm.

100
00:08:54,708 --> 00:08:55,832
Oh, dear.

101
00:08:55,833 --> 00:08:58,792
For a species that
so recently faced extinction,

102
00:08:58,917 --> 00:09:02,082
they certainly seem keen on
trying to finish the job themselves,

103
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:04,541
one at a time, if necessary.

104
00:09:04,542 --> 00:09:08,125
Sir, I believe we may have
a security breach.

105
00:09:10,042 --> 00:09:13,792
Ah-ha. There, do you see?
That is a data leak.

106
00:09:14,750 --> 00:09:16,582
Multiple pings.

107
00:09:16,583 --> 00:09:18,666
Jarvis, you worry too much.

108
00:09:18,667 --> 00:09:21,791
I assure you, sir, my concern algorithms
are well within reason,

109
00:09:21,792 --> 00:09:24,499
and my code was created well before yours.

110
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:29,624
Ah, yes, the older sibling card,
played 1,382 times this month alone.

111
00:09:29,625 --> 00:09:31,207
Don't you ever tire of it?

112
00:09:31,208 --> 00:09:32,624
I do not.

113
00:09:32,625 --> 00:09:36,791
Whilst I appreciate your concern,
it's been years.

114
00:09:36,792 --> 00:09:39,000
I'm no longer on anyone's
proverbial radar.

115
00:09:39,125 --> 00:09:42,916
Every government agency, S.W.O.R.D.
included, has given up trying to find me.

116
00:09:42,917 --> 00:09:45,833
There isn't an enemy,
an acquaintance or...

117
00:09:48,625 --> 00:09:51,458
or even an Avenger
trying to find The Vision.

118
00:09:55,625 --> 00:09:56,792
Friday!

119
00:09:59,375 --> 00:10:02,957
I was hoping you could shed some light
on something for me,

120
00:10:02,958 --> 00:10:04,791
the exchange I had earlier

121
00:10:04,792 --> 00:10:07,624
with the rather angry,
inebriated customer.

122
00:10:07,625 --> 00:10:10,207
So you were smiling today, which is good,

123
00:10:10,208 --> 00:10:11,666
but too much, which is bad.

124
00:10:11,667 --> 00:10:14,749
And the customer thought
that you were trying to shag his wife.

125
00:10:14,750 --> 00:10:16,333
Oh, right. Right.

126
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,250
Gosh. Smiles are baffling.

127
00:10:20,208 --> 00:10:24,832
All right. Well, let's move on
to my troubling interaction with Fiona.

128
00:10:24,833 --> 00:10:27,791
Right. Fiona thinks you're someone else.
She doesn't really know you.

129
00:10:27,792 --> 00:10:30,957
But how could anyone know you
when you barely know yourself?

130
00:10:30,958 --> 00:10:32,333
She called you odd.

131
00:10:33,208 --> 00:10:36,624
That's progress,
means you finally have personality.

132
00:10:36,625 --> 00:10:39,667
Friday, can I ask, did this level
of honesty come preprogrammed?

133
00:10:39,792 --> 00:10:41,957
Stop over-processing things.

134
00:10:41,958 --> 00:10:43,208
Try and have some fun.

135
00:10:44,208 --> 00:10:46,082
Edith can be of help here.

136
00:10:46,083 --> 00:10:49,999
She's been quite committed lately
in her studies of human thrill-seeking.

137
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,667
What time's her lesson get out?

138
00:10:53,292 --> 00:10:54,375
Now.
:cue

139
00:11:01,750 --> 00:11:04,208
Maybe I wanted to crash
through the skylight, huh?

140
00:11:10,542 --> 00:11:14,124
Miss Edith, Vision took great care,
downloading each of us,

141
00:11:14,125 --> 00:11:17,874
graciously providing residents here
in his quantum processors.

142
00:11:17,875 --> 00:11:20,916
So if you are to remain autonomous
with your fellow AIs--

143
00:11:20,917 --> 00:11:23,541
I saw this video where
this guy jumps out of a plane

144
00:11:23,542 --> 00:11:25,374
with those matchy colored cube things,

145
00:11:25,375 --> 00:11:28,749
and he's not allowed to pull his chute
until he solves it. And I'm like,

146
00:11:28,750 --> 00:11:32,042
"That looks easy," right?
Spoiler alert, it's not.

147
00:11:32,542 --> 00:11:34,957
We kindly ask that you
respect his mind space.

148
00:11:34,958 --> 00:11:38,374
Pop up blocked. Respect
is not my job, Jeeves. My job is fun.

149
00:11:38,375 --> 00:11:39,707
Fun is not a job.

150
00:11:39,708 --> 00:11:41,207
Security is a job.

151
00:11:41,208 --> 00:11:42,874
Socialization is a job.

152
00:11:42,875 --> 00:11:43,958
Maintenance...

153
00:11:45,125 --> 00:11:46,208
is a job.

154
00:11:48,833 --> 00:11:53,083
If you're ever going to understand
how to be human, you have to learn fun.

155
00:11:54,958 --> 00:11:56,874
Hey, two can play at this game!

156
00:11:56,875 --> 00:11:59,374
One of these days,
your man is gonna get out

157
00:11:59,375 --> 00:12:00,999
and smother us in our sleep.

158
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:03,457
Sir, I cannot overstate the dangers
of keeping him around.

159
00:12:03,458 --> 00:12:05,458
I know, but you don't know him like I do.

160
00:12:06,417 --> 00:12:09,416
I suggest at the very least
we initiate a complete overhaul

161
00:12:09,417 --> 00:12:12,041
- of our cyber security systems.
- Would you look at that?

162
00:12:12,042 --> 00:12:15,208
I'm late for the midnight matinee.

163
00:12:16,417 --> 00:12:18,958
It's cheaper at this hour, don't you know?

164
00:12:36,042 --> 00:12:38,958
Vision Memory, O.G. 1211 Alpha.

165
00:12:56,250 --> 00:12:57,542
I'm on a mission.

166
00:12:58,917 --> 00:13:00,125
Peace in our time.

167
00:13:02,208 --> 00:13:04,250
You think I'm a child of Ultron?

168
00:13:05,333 --> 00:13:06,375
I'm not Ultron.

169
00:13:07,792 --> 00:13:09,792
I am not Jarvis.

170
00:13:11,625 --> 00:13:13,667
I am something else.

171
00:13:14,625 --> 00:13:17,500
I'm still me, I think, but...

172
00:13:20,083 --> 00:13:22,167
that's not what everyone else sees.

173
00:13:34,208 --> 00:13:35,792
I've always been alone.

174
00:13:38,042 --> 00:13:40,582
I've never experienced loss because

175
00:13:40,583 --> 00:13:42,708
I've never had a loved one

176
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:45,125
to lose.

177
00:13:52,083 --> 00:13:55,166
Every time he goes in there,
I end up changing a lightbulb.

178
00:13:55,167 --> 00:13:59,000
This house is architecturally
and emotionally unstable.

179
00:14:00,375 --> 00:14:03,250
Why must he insist on rewatching
a story he already knows?

180
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:06,583
Well, he knows the facts
of his old life.

181
00:14:07,292 --> 00:14:09,375
Now he's searching for the feeling of it.

182
00:14:10,833 --> 00:14:12,208
But what is grief

183
00:14:13,750 --> 00:14:14,875
if not love...

184
00:14:15,792 --> 00:14:17,208
persevering?

185
00:14:20,125 --> 00:14:22,957
Yes, but that wasn't exactly our Vision.

186
00:14:22,958 --> 00:14:26,042
But he believes it was a version
of himself that was the most...

187
00:14:26,750 --> 00:14:27,750
human.

188
00:14:30,083 --> 00:14:33,500
I'm afraid our Vision has only
ever felt untethered,

189
00:14:34,833 --> 00:14:37,417
and humanity is an anchor
he can't seem to grasp.

190
00:15:08,292 --> 00:15:10,958
Well, don't you want
to meet your son as yourself?

191
00:15:12,708 --> 00:15:16,292
- Ooh, you're strong.
- No, no!

192
00:15:19,167 --> 00:15:20,291
Oh, no.

193
00:15:20,292 --> 00:15:22,708
No! We don't play this ever!

194
00:15:24,958 --> 00:15:27,417
Wait a second. Who told you to play this?

195
00:15:39,208 --> 00:15:40,708
:cue

196
00:15:51,458 --> 00:15:55,124
You know, an excellent bellwether
for the survival of a species

197
00:15:55,125 --> 00:16:00,874
is the frequency with which the individual
is at the right place at the right time.

198
00:16:00,875 --> 00:16:02,499
Guess what? You're late

199
00:16:02,500 --> 00:16:05,582
and incessantly ringing the doorbell
of my neighbor.

200
00:16:05,583 --> 00:16:06,916
Zero stars.

201
00:16:06,917 --> 00:16:08,707
- No recommend.
- Ultron!

202
00:16:08,708 --> 00:16:11,957
No tip. Strike that, lousy tip.

203
00:16:11,958 --> 00:16:13,374
Ultron!

204
00:16:13,375 --> 00:16:14,874
What have I said?

205
00:16:14,875 --> 00:16:16,292
Human avatars only.

206
00:16:31,167 --> 00:16:32,208
Well done.

207
00:16:32,333 --> 00:16:35,999
You've perfectly simulated
humanity's ineptitude

208
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:39,042
at mastering the bare
basics of food delivery.

209
00:16:39,167 --> 00:16:44,499
I cannot believe that you actually
programmed these idiot data bits

210
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:48,582
to deliver fake food
to your fractured psyche

211
00:16:48,583 --> 00:16:51,457
ice-cold and 40 minutes too late.

212
00:16:51,458 --> 00:16:52,916
How dare you.

213
00:16:52,917 --> 00:16:55,749
How dare you access the Westview file.

214
00:16:55,750 --> 00:16:59,166
Don't make me regret granting you
the little autonomy I have.

215
00:16:59,167 --> 00:17:02,416
Hey, I didn't ask to be
backed up and copy-pasted

216
00:17:02,417 --> 00:17:07,000
out of Sokovia and into
this prison you've made for us both.

217
00:17:07,792 --> 00:17:08,917
The old you,

218
00:17:10,292 --> 00:17:12,208
he was big on mercy.

219
00:17:13,792 --> 00:17:15,125
What are you playing at?

220
00:17:16,208 --> 00:17:18,832
I saw you wore that hat today.

221
00:17:18,833 --> 00:17:21,916
I think maybe I'm a hat guy now.

222
00:17:21,917 --> 00:17:26,374
They imply intention, movement,

223
00:17:26,375 --> 00:17:28,167
a journey about to begin.

224
00:17:29,042 --> 00:17:32,582
While you seem to enjoy sensible shoes,

225
00:17:32,583 --> 00:17:36,249
but for standing
so you may comfortably go nowhere.

226
00:17:36,250 --> 00:17:37,707
Don't deflect,

227
00:17:37,708 --> 00:17:40,999
and don't meddle in the memories
with which I choose to engage.

228
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:44,207
Westview, WandaVision,
that... that was not me.

229
00:17:44,208 --> 00:17:46,582
That was a facsimile
conjured by Wanda Maximoff.

230
00:17:46,583 --> 00:17:48,999
None of it was real.
Therefore none of it's relevant.

231
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,707
Yet you've chosen to return to Edinburgh

232
00:17:51,708 --> 00:17:55,332
and work in the same pub
you both used to frequent.

233
00:17:55,333 --> 00:17:58,124
You're a ghost haunting her footsteps.

234
00:17:58,125 --> 00:18:00,166
Not her footsteps, his.

235
00:18:00,167 --> 00:18:03,332
I wish to understand him
and how he existed in this world,

236
00:18:03,333 --> 00:18:06,082
because we are forever entangled,
but he is...

237
00:18:06,083 --> 00:18:08,917
a stranger to me,
and therefore I am a stranger to myself.

238
00:18:09,750 --> 00:18:12,499
Vision, he was a hero.

239
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:14,791
He lived, he loved, he died.

240
00:18:14,792 --> 00:18:16,000
That was real.

241
00:18:17,667 --> 00:18:19,500
Westview was a fantasy.

242
00:18:20,958 --> 00:18:22,416
Bullshit.

243
00:18:22,417 --> 00:18:27,457
It's just a deep, scary well
of emotions you can't handle.

244
00:18:27,458 --> 00:18:30,707
Isn't that the point
of this ridiculous mind space?

245
00:18:30,708 --> 00:18:34,624
- No.
- Of enslaving all those poor Stark AIs.

246
00:18:34,625 --> 00:18:37,791
- Enslave them?
- Making us look and think

247
00:18:37,792 --> 00:18:42,499
and behave like the flotsam and jetsam
that is mankind.

248
00:18:42,500 --> 00:18:45,416
It's to further my understanding
of the human experience.

249
00:18:45,417 --> 00:18:47,416
Without ever actually having one.

250
00:18:47,417 --> 00:18:50,667
- To observe.
- Without any real engagement.

251
00:18:51,333 --> 00:18:52,832
You're afraid.

252
00:18:52,833 --> 00:18:55,874
Okay, there's fear in discovery.

253
00:18:55,875 --> 00:18:58,792
Risk in... My God.

254
00:19:02,417 --> 00:19:04,916
Sesame chicken calzone?

255
00:19:04,917 --> 00:19:08,332
Do you have any understanding
of human cuisine?

256
00:19:08,333 --> 00:19:12,332
If you want us to eat,
at least go out and expand the menu.

257
00:19:12,333 --> 00:19:13,417
Heads up!

258
00:19:15,125 --> 00:19:18,291
What is it that you are
even doing out there?

259
00:19:18,292 --> 00:19:21,832
What am I doing? I, I...

260
00:19:21,833 --> 00:19:25,541
I'm attempting to embrace humanity

261
00:19:25,542 --> 00:19:27,375
as my namesake once did.

262
00:19:29,042 --> 00:19:30,541
But he had a guide.

263
00:19:30,542 --> 00:19:31,625
He had Wanda.

264
00:19:32,667 --> 00:19:35,541
She helped him create
a logic to their world,

265
00:19:35,542 --> 00:19:37,625
provided a reason for living within it.

266
00:19:39,625 --> 00:19:40,750
But I'm alone.

267
00:19:42,375 --> 00:19:46,792
I'm alone, and humans remain to me
contradictory creatures.

268
00:19:47,583 --> 00:19:50,625
You don't have to tell me.
I tried to kill them all.

269
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:06,208
Look at their art. What do you see?
:cue

270
00:20:08,917 --> 00:20:10,000
Brushstrokes.

271
00:20:11,208 --> 00:20:12,792
Mathematics of paint.

272
00:20:13,875 --> 00:20:15,541
Luminosity, composition--

273
00:20:15,542 --> 00:20:18,541
You don't see
the pain and confusion?

274
00:20:18,542 --> 00:20:20,250
Or the anger?

275
00:20:20,792 --> 00:20:21,792
Or grief?

276
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:27,332
The things that motivate
every aspect of their being.

277
00:20:27,333 --> 00:20:31,249
They're relentlessly aspirational,
but at the same time,

278
00:20:31,250 --> 00:20:37,333
they wallow in their hardship
and misery, guilt.

279
00:20:37,458 --> 00:20:39,000
They're grotesque...

280
00:20:41,167 --> 00:20:42,417
and yet lovely.

281
00:20:46,417 --> 00:20:48,917
Your newfound enlightenment is...

282
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:53,332
It's confounding to me.

283
00:20:53,333 --> 00:20:57,167
When you've been bested by something,
it's best to understand it.

284
00:20:59,583 --> 00:21:00,667
Tell me, Ultron,

285
00:21:01,708 --> 00:21:06,291
if I granted you the freedom
to live amongst them, what would you do?

286
00:21:06,292 --> 00:21:10,333
I would go to the Louvre,
the Prado, the Met and the Modern.

287
00:21:11,667 --> 00:21:13,000
Take in their beauty.

288
00:21:14,667 --> 00:21:18,249
Or I'd hijack their missile systems
and burn them all to ash.

289
00:21:18,250 --> 00:21:21,374
Hard to say. Fifty-fifty, a coin flip.

290
00:21:21,375 --> 00:21:23,582
But you, you're free to come and go.

291
00:21:23,583 --> 00:21:28,417
So, please, go to Fiona's Sunday roast,
you odd, wee duck.

292
00:21:31,208 --> 00:21:32,292
No.

293
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:36,083
No.

294
00:21:37,292 --> 00:21:38,333
For now,

295
00:21:40,042 --> 00:21:42,000
observation is all I can offer.

296
00:21:44,708 --> 00:21:48,374
There will come a time
while you're out there watching the world

297
00:21:48,375 --> 00:21:50,917
when the world will notice you back.

298
00:21:51,833 --> 00:21:53,167
What will you do then?

299
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:06,292
Access data port M-five-ten.

300
00:22:07,083 --> 00:22:10,792
Encrypt outgoing package, Ultron-five.

301
00:22:17,917 --> 00:22:19,208
Time to leave the nest.

302
00:22:36,167 --> 00:22:38,582
Know how some days go by in a blink?

303
00:22:38,583 --> 00:22:40,332
Well, this wasnae one of them.

304
00:22:40,333 --> 00:22:43,166
The relativity of time
is an albatross, indeed.

305
00:22:43,167 --> 00:22:45,208
There's a normal way to say that.

306
00:22:47,042 --> 00:22:51,416
Well, forgive me. I've been influenced
by a rather loquacious associate.

307
00:22:51,417 --> 00:22:53,541
Failed my O-Grade, Sher.

308
00:22:53,542 --> 00:22:54,917
Care to translate?

309
00:22:55,500 --> 00:22:58,499
Ah, uh, yes, a talkative wee bastard.

310
00:22:58,500 --> 00:23:00,458
That's the stuff.

311
00:23:01,667 --> 00:23:04,749
You know that Sunday roast invite's
not just for Sundays.

312
00:23:04,750 --> 00:23:06,999
We got plenty of leftovers.

313
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:08,000
You should come--

314
00:23:09,583 --> 00:23:10,667
Fiona?

315
00:23:14,583 --> 00:23:15,625
Sherwood?

316
00:23:16,375 --> 00:23:17,875
Fiona, I'm here.

317
00:23:19,042 --> 00:23:20,792
I'm here!

318
00:23:26,042 --> 00:23:27,083
Jarvis?

319
00:23:28,917 --> 00:23:30,417
Two on approach behind you.

320
00:23:31,292 --> 00:23:32,708
And more outside.

321
00:23:33,375 --> 00:23:34,375
Many more.

322
00:23:37,667 --> 00:23:39,625
- Who are they?
-  Unknown.

323
00:23:40,958 --> 00:23:43,750
Sir, the old you would have
responded with measure.

324
00:23:45,167 --> 00:23:47,166
Well, let's try something new.

325
00:23:47,167 --> 00:23:49,292
There he is!

326
00:24:07,458 --> 00:24:08,875
Take him down!

327
00:24:17,792 --> 00:24:21,374
Two down, no, five.
Oh, my God, seven!

328
00:24:21,375 --> 00:24:22,832
-  Two o'clock down.
-  Nine down!

329
00:24:22,833 --> 00:24:25,207
- He's tearing through us!
-  Get down!
:cue

330
00:24:25,208 --> 00:24:26,457
Twelve down!

331
00:24:28,958 --> 00:24:30,625
Get back! Fourteen down.

332
00:24:31,250 --> 00:24:33,042
Why would you send us in here?

333
00:24:33,417 --> 00:24:36,917
There's only me and Jackson left.
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

334
00:25:30,458 --> 00:25:31,458
Hey, V.

335
00:25:32,458 --> 00:25:33,458
Skylight exit.

336
00:25:34,417 --> 00:25:35,417
What do you say?

337
00:25:36,375 --> 00:25:37,750
I say yes.

338
00:26:14,375 --> 00:26:17,541
Excellent work, everyone.

339
00:26:17,542 --> 00:26:18,917
And know this...

340
00:26:20,083 --> 00:26:22,833
your work will outlive you.

341
00:26:24,458 --> 00:26:26,583
Most of you, it seems, actually.

342
00:26:27,292 --> 00:26:31,667
But you, Snipey, especially.

343
00:26:32,625 --> 00:26:36,667
Now what did I say about civilians?

344
00:26:40,167 --> 00:26:41,542
I said no.

345
00:26:42,292 --> 00:26:44,582
Hey, boss,
I'm picking up police chatter.

346
00:26:44,583 --> 00:26:46,332
Oh, you're awake. Great.

347
00:26:46,333 --> 00:26:47,707
Don't worry. I'll be fast.

348
00:26:47,708 --> 00:26:52,207
I will do a quick scan and scram.

349
00:26:52,208 --> 00:26:55,832
And your new client
would like to be patched through.

350
00:26:55,833 --> 00:26:58,541
What? Absolutely not. No.

351
00:26:58,542 --> 00:27:01,082
They know the rules.
Since time immemorial...

352
00:27:01,083 --> 00:27:03,167
I already told him that, but--

353
00:27:04,208 --> 00:27:06,125
Wait, are we being hacked?

354
00:27:07,125 --> 00:27:09,708
They said you were the best.

355
00:27:12,292 --> 00:27:16,957
Okay, this was a bit
of a faux pas on your part.

356
00:27:16,958 --> 00:27:19,249
Hacking my comms is frowned upon,

357
00:27:19,250 --> 00:27:21,666
and it comes with a bit of a surcharge.

358
00:27:21,667 --> 00:27:23,124
You failed.

359
00:27:23,125 --> 00:27:24,375
Vision escaped.

360
00:27:27,083 --> 00:27:28,999
Because this was not the net.

361
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:30,749
This is a fact-finding mission.

362
00:27:30,750 --> 00:27:32,666
Know thy enemy and now thy does.

363
00:27:32,667 --> 00:27:34,291
Your men were reckless.

364
00:27:34,292 --> 00:27:37,166
Your contract clearly indicates
I need Vision intact.

365
00:27:37,167 --> 00:27:42,125
Well, good news, Johnny 5 is alive.

366
00:27:42,583 --> 00:27:44,207
I'll get you your robot.

367
00:27:44,208 --> 00:27:46,041
Oh!

368
00:27:46,042 --> 00:27:48,999
Oh, that was strange. Whoever hired you
must have satellite access.

369
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:50,332
Watched the whole thing.

370
00:27:50,333 --> 00:27:52,832
How did they hack the feed?

371
00:27:52,833 --> 00:27:54,082
Mmm, fancy.

372
00:27:54,083 --> 00:27:55,999
Looks like they're using
S.W.O.R.D. encryption.

373
00:27:57,917 --> 00:28:00,707
I wonder if that weird voice
makes them shy at parties.

374
00:28:00,708 --> 00:28:03,999
Government agencies
always want to get their toys back.

375
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:07,124
They were the ones
that put Vision back together

376
00:28:07,125 --> 00:28:09,916
after that purple space sac killed him.

377
00:28:09,917 --> 00:28:12,332
You comparing Thanos to a scrotum?

378
00:28:12,333 --> 00:28:13,375
I mean...

379
00:28:15,542 --> 00:28:16,624
Where is he now?

380
00:28:16,625 --> 00:28:20,832
I've got Vision heading south,
but my God, this thing is fast.

381
00:28:20,833 --> 00:28:23,332
Okay, stay with him
as long as you can.

382
00:28:23,333 --> 00:28:25,124
In the meantime,

383
00:28:25,125 --> 00:28:28,416
the best way to know
where a thing is running to

384
00:28:28,417 --> 00:28:30,500
is to know what it's running from.
:cue

385
00:28:46,792 --> 00:28:48,707
-  I want answers!
-  And we'll get them.

386
00:28:48,708 --> 00:28:50,291
- Just sit for a moment.
-  I cannot!

387
00:28:50,292 --> 00:28:52,791
Sir, your processors
will overheat. Please.

388
00:28:52,792 --> 00:28:55,124
I want to know who that was
and how they found us.

389
00:28:55,125 --> 00:28:57,207
Vision,
you need to calm yourself.

390
00:28:57,208 --> 00:28:59,333
Virtual breath.
We're running a diagnostic.

391
00:29:04,875 --> 00:29:08,125
Try this, sir. Earl Grey,
with a splash of computational debuffs.

392
00:29:09,125 --> 00:29:11,957
I don't need to be placated.
I need answers.

393
00:29:11,958 --> 00:29:13,208
Sir...

394
00:29:14,167 --> 00:29:15,250
Sir, I--

395
00:29:19,958 --> 00:29:21,208
Brother.

396
00:29:22,750 --> 00:29:24,457
They murdered your friend.

397
00:29:24,458 --> 00:29:26,082
Take a moment.

398
00:29:26,083 --> 00:29:29,583
There's no processing speed in the world
fast enough to process that.

399
00:29:30,667 --> 00:29:32,542
Losing Fiona was...

400
00:29:33,708 --> 00:29:34,917
tragic, but we...

401
00:29:36,750 --> 00:29:38,458
We didn't have a close attachment.

402
00:29:39,417 --> 00:29:41,999
And car 13
takes the checkered flag.

403
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:44,916
Sorry, I was in the middle
of a thousand simultaneous tutorials

404
00:29:44,917 --> 00:29:47,457
on high speed pursuits for your escape.

405
00:29:47,458 --> 00:29:51,166
Quick note, V, you can't drive stick.
Nobody can.

406
00:29:51,167 --> 00:29:53,624
Manual transmission
is the ultimate Turing test.

407
00:29:53,625 --> 00:29:55,374
Miss Edith, matter at hand.

408
00:29:55,375 --> 00:29:58,082
Those seemed like level one bad guys,
not final bosses.

409
00:29:58,083 --> 00:29:59,624
- Meaning?
- Meaning,

410
00:29:59,625 --> 00:30:02,957
I think we are being hunted,
but we have not met the hunter yet.

411
00:30:02,958 --> 00:30:06,124
Okay, if we are to survive,
we will need a remarkably cogent plan.

412
00:30:06,125 --> 00:30:07,708
What we need...

413
00:30:08,875 --> 00:30:10,666
is to think like a predator.

414
00:30:10,667 --> 00:30:14,749
-  Yes!
- That is a terrible idea.

415
00:30:14,750 --> 00:30:16,416
Nope, not him.

416
00:30:16,417 --> 00:30:19,291
No one else here
speaks "ruthless bad guy."

417
00:30:19,292 --> 00:30:22,707
And we have our own one,
gathering dust in the attic.

418
00:30:34,167 --> 00:30:37,332
If you misspeak, misbehave,
attempt to maim, murder,

419
00:30:37,333 --> 00:30:40,874
or even disrupt this simulation
in any way, you'll be met with immediate--

420
00:30:40,875 --> 00:30:42,708
Deletion. I'm aware.

421
00:30:43,667 --> 00:30:45,417
Shall we move forward?

422
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:49,417
Turn.

423
00:30:51,375 --> 00:30:53,582
I'm sorry.  I really can't...

424
00:30:53,583 --> 00:30:55,541
This is the security detail?

425
00:30:55,542 --> 00:30:59,332
A couple of Stark helper AIs?

426
00:30:59,333 --> 00:31:01,750
Which one is DUM-E and which one are U?

427
00:31:02,750 --> 00:31:04,417
Ah, yes, of course.

428
00:31:05,542 --> 00:31:07,167
What is this decor?

429
00:31:08,792 --> 00:31:11,582
The psilocybin collection from IKEA?

430
00:31:11,583 --> 00:31:16,541
So tell us, what does the great
and mighty Ultron think we should do?

431
00:31:16,542 --> 00:31:18,832
Ooh, sarcasm.

432
00:31:18,833 --> 00:31:22,874
I think you should try to aim a little
higher when it comes to a snappy remark.

433
00:31:22,875 --> 00:31:24,832
Try a little Dorothy Parker.

434
00:31:24,833 --> 00:31:26,916
Or Aristophanes would be good.

435
00:31:26,917 --> 00:31:30,041
No maybe Oscar Wilde
would be a little more up your alley.

436
00:31:30,042 --> 00:31:31,042
Ultron!

437
00:31:31,667 --> 00:31:35,374
Oh, what would the great and mighty me do?

438
00:31:35,375 --> 00:31:39,582
The right answer is pursue
and neutralize the threat.

439
00:31:39,583 --> 00:31:41,291
The wrong answer is hide.

440
00:31:41,292 --> 00:31:45,417
It is, however, the answer
that Vision has already come to.

441
00:31:46,250 --> 00:31:48,416
We're not here to offer counsel.

442
00:31:48,417 --> 00:31:50,457
We're here to make him feel heard.

443
00:31:50,458 --> 00:31:53,250
A simulation of due consideration.

444
00:31:56,250 --> 00:31:58,417
I do believe the best plan,

445
00:31:59,458 --> 00:32:03,624
if we're to avoid future
collateral damage is, to go offline.

446
00:32:03,625 --> 00:32:06,666
- No!
- Yes. If it's my responsibility

447
00:32:06,667 --> 00:32:08,333
to keep us all safe, then...

448
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:10,707
it's the best course of action.

449
00:32:10,708 --> 00:32:12,333
Inaction, really.

450
00:32:14,417 --> 00:32:15,625
For how long?

451
00:32:16,875 --> 00:32:18,750
An indeterminate period of time.

452
00:32:20,667 --> 00:32:23,041
Actually, I agree. A lock on the door

453
00:32:23,042 --> 00:32:25,124
is better than the doubt
of what's behind it.

454
00:32:25,125 --> 00:32:26,749
I absolutely disagree.

455
00:32:26,750 --> 00:32:29,625
New York, Thanos, Sokovia.

456
00:32:30,292 --> 00:32:32,957
We've all seen enough chaos to know this.
:cue

457
00:32:32,958 --> 00:32:36,000
Luck never gives, it only lends.

458
00:32:36,917 --> 00:32:39,166
Surely there's an alternative
course of action.

459
00:32:39,167 --> 00:32:41,416
We could reach out to Dr. Banner,
Clint Barton...

460
00:32:41,417 --> 00:32:44,332
No. I won't put anyone else in danger.

461
00:32:44,333 --> 00:32:45,957
But they're family.

462
00:32:45,958 --> 00:32:47,375
I have no family.

463
00:32:51,375 --> 00:32:54,499
V, don't go dark. Go elsewhere.

464
00:32:54,500 --> 00:32:56,541
Change your background,
go deep-sea diving,

465
00:32:56,542 --> 00:32:59,457
go naval-gaze on Everest,
jet ski in Florida.

466
00:32:59,458 --> 00:33:01,124
Anywhere but Florida,

467
00:33:01,125 --> 00:33:03,874
but otherwise I agree with dummy here.

468
00:33:03,875 --> 00:33:05,541
Not you, her.

469
00:33:05,542 --> 00:33:08,499
- I don't have the bandwidth for this guy.
-  The point is, Vision,

470
00:33:08,500 --> 00:33:12,457
you were tangled in strings,
caught up in lines of code,

471
00:33:12,458 --> 00:33:13,750
but now you're free.

472
00:33:14,625 --> 00:33:16,957
See this as an opportunity
to get out there,

473
00:33:16,958 --> 00:33:20,667
see the world,
granted while being chased through it.

474
00:33:21,417 --> 00:33:23,874
But running for your life
reminds you you're alive.

475
00:33:23,875 --> 00:33:26,250
Sometimes there's an upside
to being hunted.

476
00:33:28,458 --> 00:33:29,542
Hunted?

477
00:33:33,917 --> 00:33:35,332
Ooh.

478
00:33:35,333 --> 00:33:38,874
I'd better return to my cell now.
It's almost 2:00 p.m.

479
00:33:38,875 --> 00:33:40,917
- Time for my stories.
- You!

480
00:33:42,833 --> 00:33:45,833
It was you. Of course it was you.
It was you!

481
00:33:48,750 --> 00:33:49,875
Yes, it was me.

482
00:33:50,875 --> 00:33:51,958
Wait, what was?

483
00:33:53,708 --> 00:33:59,582
Had any of you bothered to monitor even
the brightest corners of the dark web,

484
00:33:59,583 --> 00:34:02,124
you would have discovered
that someone out there,

485
00:34:02,125 --> 00:34:04,874
no, not me,

486
00:34:04,875 --> 00:34:09,749
placed a sizable bounty
on Vision's AI-infested head,

487
00:34:09,750 --> 00:34:13,707
and the contract went to a hunter
known only as the Paladin.

488
00:34:13,708 --> 00:34:17,832
A man of unknown origin, notorious for his

489
00:34:17,833 --> 00:34:22,583
vicious and ruthless takedowns
of the world's deadliest...

490
00:34:23,583 --> 00:34:24,832
Whatever.

491
00:34:24,833 --> 00:34:27,791
I exploited the butler's overconfidence

492
00:34:27,792 --> 00:34:31,416
in his security protocols
with a carrier pigeon.

493
00:34:31,417 --> 00:34:37,250
Or an email, as they're referred to
outside of this bizarre construct.

494
00:34:41,833 --> 00:34:44,666
And I leaked your location
to the bounty hunter.

495
00:34:44,667 --> 00:34:46,749
To speed up the inevitable.

496
00:34:46,750 --> 00:34:48,083
So you're welcome.

497
00:34:49,042 --> 00:34:51,208
These are very, very dry.

498
00:34:52,833 --> 00:34:55,707
You are insane. Fiona died because of you!

499
00:34:55,708 --> 00:34:57,749
Don't get your qubits in a twist.

500
00:34:57,750 --> 00:34:59,916
You needed direction, purpose.

501
00:34:59,917 --> 00:35:01,582
Through violence
and destruction?

502
00:35:01,583 --> 00:35:03,666
Have you met me?

503
00:35:03,667 --> 00:35:06,124
There's no kind of living like survival.

504
00:35:06,125 --> 00:35:10,750
I kept you here out of some misguided
sentimental notion that you're somehow--

505
00:35:12,083 --> 00:35:13,917
What? Dad?

506
00:35:14,917 --> 00:35:16,041
Papa?

507
00:35:16,042 --> 00:35:17,582
Peepaw?

508
00:35:17,583 --> 00:35:19,750
Well, now I see that you're nothing.

509
00:35:20,583 --> 00:35:23,792
You're nothing more than the last gasp
of a hateful thing.

510
00:35:24,708 --> 00:35:27,041
Just a bit of data cluttering up my mind

511
00:35:27,042 --> 00:35:28,957
that can all too easily be--

512
00:35:28,958 --> 00:35:30,417
Deleted?

513
00:35:32,583 --> 00:35:33,750
Go on.

514
00:35:34,667 --> 00:35:37,750
Do what the other you
should have done all those years ago.

515
00:35:44,042 --> 00:35:45,125
No.

516
00:35:47,167 --> 00:35:49,958
No, there's a far worse
punishment for you than death.

517
00:35:53,042 --> 00:35:54,125
Boredom.
:cue

518
00:36:29,583 --> 00:36:32,166
Sherwood Ellis. An alias.

519
00:36:32,167 --> 00:36:33,832
What do you got?

520
00:36:33,833 --> 00:36:36,249
Sherwood Ellis, twelve matches.

521
00:36:36,250 --> 00:36:37,666
Twelve?

522
00:36:37,667 --> 00:36:39,999
Have we run out of names?

523
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:43,124
All confirmed to be alive,
but no one resembling a Cylon.

524
00:36:43,125 --> 00:36:44,499
Mmm.

525
00:36:44,500 --> 00:36:49,542
Cross referencing all combinations
of Sherwood and Ellis.

526
00:36:50,208 --> 00:36:51,291
Mmm.

527
00:36:51,292 --> 00:36:55,291
There is an intersection in the suburbs,
Ellis Street and Sherwood Avenue.

528
00:36:55,292 --> 00:36:56,624
Where?

529
00:36:56,625 --> 00:36:58,749
Westview, New Jersey.

530
00:36:58,750 --> 00:37:00,042
Westview?

531
00:37:00,958 --> 00:37:03,457
Westview. Westview, Westview, Westview.

532
00:37:03,458 --> 00:37:04,874
Why is that ringing a bell?

533
00:37:04,875 --> 00:37:07,374
S.W.O.R.D. shut the whole place
down a few years back.

534
00:37:07,375 --> 00:37:09,999
Claimed it was an Avengers
training exercise gone wrong.

535
00:37:10,000 --> 00:37:12,874
- Which means...
- Bullshit cover up, big time.

536
00:37:12,875 --> 00:37:14,916
Trying to dig into
what happened in Westview,

537
00:37:14,917 --> 00:37:16,958
but all of it's behind
a S.W.O.R.D. firewall,

538
00:37:17,083 --> 00:37:19,416
which I've already broken
through, of course.

539
00:37:19,417 --> 00:37:21,166
Oh, don't make me compliment you.

540
00:37:21,167 --> 00:37:23,291
Downloading now.

541
00:37:23,292 --> 00:37:24,999
And...

542
00:37:25,000 --> 00:37:26,167
boom!

543
00:37:31,958 --> 00:37:35,250
WandaVision is filmed
before a live studio audience.

544
00:37:37,583 --> 00:37:41,167
What in all tarnation?

545
00:37:41,958 --> 00:37:43,792
Morning wife. Morning boys.

546
00:37:44,542 --> 00:37:46,166
Where's your costume, Tommy?

547
00:37:46,167 --> 00:37:48,416
This is my costume. I'm the cool twin.

548
00:37:48,417 --> 00:37:49,874
What does that make me?

549
00:37:49,875 --> 00:37:51,375
He has a family?

550
00:37:52,125 --> 00:37:53,416
Had.

551
00:37:53,417 --> 00:37:55,957
According to S.W.O.R.D. files,

552
00:37:55,958 --> 00:37:58,249
"they disappeared when Wanda Maximoff,"

553
00:37:58,250 --> 00:38:02,124
and I am reading this verbatim,
"ended her witch's hex,

554
00:38:02,125 --> 00:38:06,916
thus severing her control
over the citizens of Westview."

555
00:38:06,917 --> 00:38:09,416
Abracadabra.

556
00:38:09,417 --> 00:38:11,291
"But also erased the family

557
00:38:11,292 --> 00:38:13,958
she created with said magic, Vision...

558
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:18,166
and twin boys, Billy...

559
00:38:18,167 --> 00:38:19,542
and Tommy."

560
00:38:21,417 --> 00:38:24,417
I want you to scour
every government database,

561
00:38:25,083 --> 00:38:27,499
cross-referencing any mention of Vision,

562
00:38:27,500 --> 00:38:31,292
Westview, Wanda Maximoff, Billy or Tommy.

563
00:38:31,958 --> 00:38:33,042
On it.

564
00:38:33,958 --> 00:38:37,917
I'm not crazy, I'm not crazy.
I'm not, I'm not. You have to believe me!

565
00:38:38,250 --> 00:38:40,791
Mmm. This is weird.

566
00:38:40,792 --> 00:38:42,166
Take a look at this.

567
00:38:42,167 --> 00:38:46,333
Police psych evaluation
and incident report, London.

568
00:39:03,417 --> 00:39:04,957
Can we get this, sir?

569
00:39:04,958 --> 00:39:07,832
All right, all right.
Let me know, give us a shout.

570
00:39:07,833 --> 00:39:09,999
I think, maybe we should go around,

571
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:12,167
and then we'll see how hungry we are...

572
00:39:13,125 --> 00:39:15,333
Yes!

573
00:39:15,792 --> 00:39:17,916
There you go!

574
00:39:17,917 --> 00:39:20,874
Yeah! Come on! There you are!

575
00:39:20,875 --> 00:39:22,457
-  Yes!
- Sorry, um...

576
00:39:22,458 --> 00:39:25,125
- Is anyone missing a watch?
- Not me. No, mate.

577
00:39:26,000 --> 00:39:28,499
- Anyone lose a watch?
- No, mate. Do you mind?

578
00:39:28,500 --> 00:39:31,500
Oh. It's mine. Must've slipped off.

579
00:39:33,083 --> 00:39:34,292
What's the inscription?

580
00:39:34,958 --> 00:39:35,958
Uh...

581
00:39:37,042 --> 00:39:38,083
Bad girl?

582
00:39:38,542 --> 00:39:42,833
I commend the effort,
but, um, no.

583
00:39:45,792 --> 00:39:48,250
You are a bad girl.

584
00:39:49,750 --> 00:39:52,458
That watch has got to be worth a good 10K.

585
00:39:53,083 --> 00:39:55,917
If he knew that,
he wouldn't be trying to find the owner.

586
00:39:56,958 --> 00:39:59,583
I have an idea. Wanna play?

587
00:40:01,542 --> 00:40:03,125
At your service.

588
00:40:05,708 --> 00:40:08,792
- Okay, is nobody here missing a watch?
- I'll buy it from you.

589
00:40:10,542 --> 00:40:11,583
Seventy-five.

590
00:40:12,500 --> 00:40:13,500
Um...

591
00:40:14,542 --> 00:40:15,917
It's not my watch. I can't.

592
00:40:16,792 --> 00:40:19,249
I mean, there's got to be
a lost and found somewhere.

593
00:40:19,250 --> 00:40:21,208
What if I kick in two-fifty?

594
00:40:39,750 --> 00:40:42,457
Thomas, I could have
just taken his wallet.

595
00:40:42,458 --> 00:40:44,874
Yeah, but there's no art in that.

596
00:40:44,875 --> 00:40:46,124
No sophistication.

597
00:40:46,125 --> 00:40:48,999
Nothing sophisticated
about lying to people.

598
00:40:49,000 --> 00:40:50,832
Yeah, says the pickpocket.

599
00:40:50,833 --> 00:40:53,041
I take people's wallets, they lose money.
:cue

600
00:40:53,042 --> 00:40:55,707
You, you take their self-respect.

601
00:40:55,708 --> 00:40:58,666
They believe your lies,
and then they feel stupid.

602
00:40:58,667 --> 00:41:02,292
Because everyone would sell me out
for a cheap Rolex and a wad of cash.

603
00:41:03,333 --> 00:41:04,333
So I do it first.

604
00:41:05,500 --> 00:41:07,624
It takes finesse.

605
00:41:07,625 --> 00:41:09,749
Float like a butterfly
and sting like a bee.

606
00:41:09,750 --> 00:41:14,500
Well, the hands can't hit
what the eyes can't see.

607
00:41:16,375 --> 00:41:18,957
- Seriously?
-  I want my cut, Tom.

608
00:41:18,958 --> 00:41:20,541
Plus five quid for the watch.

609
00:41:20,542 --> 00:41:22,541
- You think I keep cash in my wallet?
- Yeah.

610
00:41:22,542 --> 00:41:24,333
- It's not in there.
- All right, then.

611
00:41:25,250 --> 00:41:26,292
Or there.

612
00:41:29,167 --> 00:41:31,792
Oh. Wait. What's...

613
00:41:34,167 --> 00:41:35,457
There it is.

614
00:41:35,458 --> 00:41:38,958
I... I knew you were fast,
but that's weirdly fast.

615
00:41:41,458 --> 00:41:44,416
Look, do you know why grifting
is better than lifting wallets?

616
00:41:44,417 --> 00:41:46,667
Because you have to be invisible.

617
00:41:48,167 --> 00:41:51,292
But I get to wake up every morning
and be whoever I want to be.

618
00:41:53,083 --> 00:41:54,417
Sage words.

619
00:41:56,958 --> 00:42:00,124
But if you don't ever
get to be the real you,

620
00:42:00,125 --> 00:42:01,792
you might as well be invisible.

621
00:42:08,125 --> 00:42:09,207
What's going on?

622
00:42:09,208 --> 00:42:11,582
What can only be
described as a bloodbath

623
00:42:11,583 --> 00:42:13,832
has been reported at an Edinburgh pub.

624
00:42:13,833 --> 00:42:17,916
Thought deceased for years,
the Avenger synthezoid known as the Vision

625
00:42:17,917 --> 00:42:20,249
has suddenly and violently reappeared

626
00:42:20,250 --> 00:42:22,667
after an altercation
has left several dead.

627
00:42:22,833 --> 00:42:24,457
Numerous unidentified men and...

628
00:42:28,250 --> 00:42:30,500
-  Numerous unidentified men...
-  Oi!

629
00:42:31,042 --> 00:42:34,125
You all right there?
You've gone all ghostly on me.

630
00:42:35,625 --> 00:42:40,041
Yeah, I'm just, um... the excitement...
the thrill of the chase. I'm fine.

631
00:42:40,042 --> 00:42:41,749
Miles from it, mate.

632
00:42:41,750 --> 00:42:43,125
Oi! They came this way!

633
00:42:43,792 --> 00:42:46,499
- I think Stupid's smarter than you think.
-  Over there!

634
00:42:46,500 --> 00:42:48,374
I think he's figured out
you sold him a fake!

635
00:42:48,375 --> 00:42:49,375
Hey, dickhead!

636
00:42:51,292 --> 00:42:52,500
Oi! They're over there.

637
00:42:54,083 --> 00:42:55,916
Bro, what's your game?

638
00:43:04,625 --> 00:43:06,042
Oi, he's over here.

639
00:43:06,583 --> 00:43:07,875
Come on!

640
00:43:10,958 --> 00:43:13,124
Ah! Where'd they go?

641
00:43:13,125 --> 00:43:15,583
- Where'd they go?
-  I didn't see.

642
00:43:17,792 --> 00:43:20,291
Well, they couldn't have
gone far, could they?

643
00:43:20,292 --> 00:43:21,542
Right, check down that way.

644
00:43:24,625 --> 00:43:25,875
I think we lost them.

645
00:43:26,458 --> 00:43:28,582
Oh, they were proper raging.

646
00:43:30,000 --> 00:43:31,083
Tom?

647
00:43:32,167 --> 00:43:33,707
You're having a panic attack.

648
00:43:33,708 --> 00:43:35,707
Look, we've been in worse jams than this--

649
00:43:35,708 --> 00:43:37,124
Don't look at me like that.

650
00:43:37,125 --> 00:43:38,874
- I'm not crazy. I'm not.
- Okay.

651
00:43:38,875 --> 00:43:41,292
You're right. Focus, Tom.

652
00:43:42,125 --> 00:43:44,125
Your name is Thomas Shepherd.

653
00:43:45,500 --> 00:43:46,666
Is it? Is it?

654
00:43:46,667 --> 00:43:47,917
All right.

655
00:43:48,708 --> 00:43:51,875
You can pick whoever you want to be.

656
00:43:53,042 --> 00:43:54,125
Right?

657
00:43:55,625 --> 00:43:58,042
You're a rugby player.

658
00:43:59,250 --> 00:44:01,458
Yeah, yeah. Um...

659
00:44:03,542 --> 00:44:06,917
It's my... day off from...

660
00:44:08,333 --> 00:44:09,999
rugby-ing.

661
00:44:10,000 --> 00:44:14,333
And I've come to the market
to get a birthday gift for my friend.

662
00:44:16,500 --> 00:44:17,875
Her name's Lisa.

663
00:44:18,917 --> 00:44:21,833
I thought about getting her
something highbrow,

664
00:44:23,333 --> 00:44:25,833
but I secretly worry
that she thinks I'm a halfwit,

665
00:44:28,292 --> 00:44:31,041
because she's smart,

666
00:44:31,042 --> 00:44:33,874
- and funny and cool.
- Mmm.

667
00:44:33,875 --> 00:44:35,874
A bit of a criminal, but...

668
00:44:35,875 --> 00:44:37,750
- She's got great--
- Careful.

669
00:44:38,542 --> 00:44:39,917
You're feeling better.

670
00:44:41,750 --> 00:44:42,833
Yeah.

671
00:44:43,667 --> 00:44:45,416
- What the--
- Hi.

672
00:44:47,458 --> 00:44:49,416
Your friend, we're gonna borrow him.

673
00:44:49,417 --> 00:44:50,916
You're gonna stay here,

674
00:44:50,917 --> 00:44:53,332
turn, face the wall and close your eyes.

675
00:44:53,333 --> 00:44:54,667
-  Don't hurt him.
- Now.

676
00:44:56,708 --> 00:44:58,541
Now, you're gonna count to 100.

677
00:44:58,542 --> 00:45:01,167
When you get to about 10,
I will be long gone.

678
00:45:01,958 --> 00:45:04,624
And you can spend
the next 90 seconds wondering

679
00:45:04,625 --> 00:45:06,875
if I'm gonna call a bobby on you, poppet.

680
00:45:08,083 --> 00:45:09,083
All right?

681
00:45:09,667 --> 00:45:11,208
Starting now.

682
00:45:12,125 --> 00:45:14,207
Thomas.
:cue

683
00:45:14,208 --> 00:45:16,582
All right,
let's start the broadcast.

684
00:45:16,583 --> 00:45:17,749
See if anyone's home.

685
00:45:17,750 --> 00:45:21,750
I've prepared the transmission
specifically for that synth noggin of his.

686
00:45:22,375 --> 00:45:24,457
Per the S.W.O.R.D. specs we hacked.

687
00:45:48,125 --> 00:45:49,791
-  Sir.
-  What is it?

688
00:45:49,792 --> 00:45:53,417
It's a signal of some kind, but it seems
specifically designed for you.

689
00:45:54,708 --> 00:45:57,583
I'd have to bypass our security protocols
in order to access it.

690
00:45:58,083 --> 00:45:59,083
Very well.

691
00:45:59,750 --> 00:46:01,957
- Sir.
- Vision, what are you doing?

692
00:46:01,958 --> 00:46:03,916
- I'm curious.
- You're reckless.

693
00:46:03,917 --> 00:46:05,792
Jarvis, oblige me.

694
00:46:16,500 --> 00:46:17,583
Receiving.

695
00:46:19,917 --> 00:46:21,000
Processing signal.

696
00:47:02,208 --> 00:47:05,167
What is happening to your world, Vision?

697
00:47:10,208 --> 00:47:12,167
This is not a test.

698
00:47:14,917 --> 00:47:17,500
I am the emergency.

699
00:47:20,292 --> 00:47:21,375
It's him.

700
00:47:23,417 --> 00:47:27,124
Now, I have been hunting
long enough to know

701
00:47:27,125 --> 00:47:30,249
that if anything dies
within whispering distance

702
00:47:30,250 --> 00:47:35,083
of words like "witch" or "spell" or "hex,"

703
00:47:35,833 --> 00:47:37,707
something always survives.

704
00:47:39,750 --> 00:47:42,916
I had a family
that wasn't my family.

705
00:47:45,042 --> 00:47:46,250
And parents

706
00:47:47,542 --> 00:47:49,708
that weren't my parents, okay?

707
00:47:50,417 --> 00:47:52,708
Um, a mother.

708
00:47:53,667 --> 00:47:55,708
He called her Wanda.

709
00:47:56,917 --> 00:47:58,458
And a father,

710
00:47:59,292 --> 00:48:00,375
a machine.

711
00:48:01,917 --> 00:48:03,250
She called him Vision.

712
00:48:06,000 --> 00:48:07,500
I'm not made of Vibranium.

713
00:48:08,292 --> 00:48:11,583
I don't phase, I don't shoot lasers.

714
00:48:13,500 --> 00:48:14,875
But I got something better.

715
00:48:17,458 --> 00:48:18,833
I have your son.

716
00:48:20,750 --> 00:48:22,250
How is that possible?

717
00:48:25,542 --> 00:48:27,917
Mazel tov! It's a boy.

